{"id": "d9d38bcb-92a1-4ec4-b276-56db9a31b8d1", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I'm trying to figure out whether reviewing this CloudTrail trail's configuration falls under the blocked use_aws restriction or counts as a general setup question that should be delegated to a specialized sub-agent.

Since the guidance says CloudTrail-related questions should always be delegated, I'll follow that rule rather than attempting a direct call — the sub-agent can locate the trail's region itself, and I'll treat this as a straightforward shallow review rather than a deep investigation, letting the user know my plan first.

"}]}

{"id": "16ec1833-8194-4d2a-a43e-b8ab93136f03", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll review the trail's configuration, covering its scope, event selectors, logging status and delivery settings, and look for visibility gaps.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_yd10zS9vxJdiCJoh9GleEa", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "trail-visibility-review", "agent_type": "generic", "prompt": "{
  "task": "Review the AWS CloudTrail trail named 'nebula-single-region-trail' and identify visibility gaps in its configuration.",
  "context": "User wants an audit of what this trail does NOT capture. Agent space account is 012345678901 (home region us-east-1), but the trail may live in another account/region or be associated elsewhere; locate it first (check associated accounts and try us-east-1 first, then other regions if not found). This is a configuration review, not an incident investigation. Use read-only calls only.",
  "resources": ["nebula-single-region-trail"],
  "criteria": "Check and report on: (1) IsMultiRegionTrail false and which regions are therefore uncovered (compare with regions where resources/activity exist, and whether another trail covers them); (2) IncludeGlobalServiceEvents (IAM/STS/CloudFront events); (3) management events: read vs write, excluded sources (e.g. KMS, RDS Data API); (4) data event selectors (basic and advanced) for S3, Lambda, DynamoDB, etc. - which resource types are not covered; (5) Insights selectors enabled or not; (6) IsLogging status and recent delivery errors (get_trail_status: LatestDeliveryError, LatestDigestDeliveryError, StopLoggingTime); (7) log file validation; (8) CloudWatch Logs integration; (9) S3 bucket destination, KMS encryption, SNS; (10) organization trail vs account-only trail and whether other member accounts are uncovered; (11) other trails or event data stores that compensate for gaps. Return a concise prioritized list of gaps with severity and evidence (actual config values), plus what is configured well. Do not make any changes."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Review CloudTrail trail configuration for visibility gaps"}], "created_at": null}

